// W2 acceptance (4a): a state that WAITS on a timer which FIRES — it must
// NOT be flagged as a deadlock (the Doc 08 §13 / Doc 30 §4.1 foot-gun
// guard). `Warming` has NO declared-event transition — its only exit is
// `after 2000 ms -> Ready`. A naive "no enabled event ⇒ deadlock" rule
// (the W1 limitation) would FALSE-POSITIVE this. The W2 explorer drives
// the timer-fire edge via `Interpreter::advance_clock`, so `Warming`
// progresses to `Ready`, then `Ready --after 1000 ms-> Done` (final).
//
// Expected: ProvenNoDeadlock, every state reachable, finite (the
// clock-origin normalisation makes the timer-cycle-free machine converge).
// Cross-checked: a direct Interpreter `advance_clock` reaches `Ready`.
language fsm 2.0

feature timers

machine Heater {
    events { }

    initial Warming

    state Warming {
        after 2000 ms -> Ready
    }

    state Ready {
        after 1000 ms -> Done
    }

    final Done
}
